{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04T3", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ec81b48964ac1ef7e77db00ac207ee44fc354592de41d73b4b7e22176cbe4452", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can use the previous very abstract lemma to produce\npresentations.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:abd0c0fd80668d5ea3db904a2e9f9379b765f47e6912923256019c6dc247c0c1", "unit_id": "tag:04T3:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04T3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f : \\mathcal{S}_U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0009": "$f_{can} : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$s$", "MATH_0013": "$t$", "MATH_0014": "$1$", "MATH_0015": "$f_{can} : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-map-space-into-stack}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stack-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ae32b284fabe9f7e8354945f07207ec19b866f45b7c936a49fa0b38950cbc3c9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fdeac099f5e9a8be6d86ff5a49abeb02013cdbde1b642241e6acc9d39b99007f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an algebraic stack over <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0006>.\nLet <MATH_0007> be a surjective smooth morphism.\nLet <MATH_0008> be the groupoid in algebraic spaces\nand <MATH_0009> be the result of applying\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto <MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011>. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the morphisms <MATH_0012>, <MATH_0013> are smooth, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the <MATH_0014>-morphism <MATH_0015>\nis an equivalence.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e31cd8d55f15a15888a72515a522b871d2f12b792304274272172820eb6b03c5", "unit_id": "tag:04T5:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04T3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$s, t$", "MATH_0002": "$1$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$a \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{X}_T)$", "MATH_0006": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0007": "$a|_T'$", "MATH_0008": "$[U/R]_{T'}$", "MATH_0009": "$f_{can} : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$[U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-property-morphism-equivalent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-map-presheaves-representable-by-spaces-transformation-property}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-characterize-essentially-surjective-when-ff}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:950b7ea346eb4b70ec84847735f741471229e6c59d7dacfbd4b41880304608ae", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:25a41c235f4fd96be29c1283c41d12c0e8d8f4f57838d9bbf4fa6f4fbacda78a", "source_text": "The morphisms <MATH_0001> are smooth by\nLemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nAs the <MATH_0002>-morphism <MATH_0003> is smooth and\nsurjective it is clear that given any scheme <MATH_0004> and any object\n<MATH_0005> there exists a smooth and surjective\nmorphism <MATH_0006> such that <MATH_0007> comes from an object of\n<MATH_0008>. Since <MATH_0009>\nis fully faithful, we deduce that\n<MATH_0010> is essentially surjective as\ndescent data on objects are effective on both sides, see\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e79aad02cd7e3d692f98c286241e7406597ac3bc69a267a1ce14f2c7c9cf88bf", "unit_id": "tag:04T5:proof"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "04T3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{S}_U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$f_{can} : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$s$", "MATH_0004": "$t$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-stack-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-flat-fp-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:43fa8db5af1daf9229be6017a60861523f6b4b4b3ebb340e38465f8615720d81", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:47c32a09c5b7ed0ee77ecb565ae631ed464302d9da434eef7d83e82b5e016b2e", "source_text": "If the morphism <MATH_0001> of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nis only assumed surjective, flat and locally of finite presentation, then\nit will still be the case that <MATH_0002> is an\nequivalence. In this case the morphisms <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> will be flat and\nlocally of finite presentation, but of course not smooth in general.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:63788f2aeb786495640c53fa6457b8f194dc1eb58b405d419b164b11920f955b", "unit_id": "tag:04WY:statement"}
